    "image_with_text_qkhXBT": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_g9qYF9": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Your cat doesn't <strong>always show that it's in pain.</strong>",
            "title_highlight_color": "#000000",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_8zCHCe": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Cats are masters at hiding pain. Dental problems often only become noticeable when they have become serious – bad breath, tartar, or the cat starting to avoid food.<br/><br/><strong>In fact, over 80% of all cats over two years</strong> of age have some form of dental problem. Untreated tartar and gum inflammation can spread bacteria to the heart, kidneys, and liver – <strong>and shorten your cat's life by several years.</strong></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_g9qYF9",
        "text_8zCHCe"
