    "image_with_text_zr8D4w": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_V9bNdh": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why Plaque<strong> Keeps Getting Worse</strong>",
            "title_highlight_color": "#47b5e9",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_ct6YMT": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most owners try dental treats, powders, or water additives. But the plaque keeps building up...</p><p><br/>Here's the problem:<strong> most solutions only clean the surface</strong>. They can't remove the bacterial plaque before it hardens into tartar.</p><p><br/>Toothbrushes? <strong>They trigger the Jacobson's organ</strong>—instant biting and scratching. Treats? Cats bite and swallow—they don't scrub. Powders and liquids? <strong>They can't scrub plaque off.</strong></p><p><br/>FreshWipes work differently. The <strong>textured surface physically scrubs plaque off</strong>. Antibacterial ingredients prevent regrowth.<br/></p><p><strong>30 seconds a day removes bacteria at the source.</strong> No bacteria, no plaque.<br/>Requires daily use for best results.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
