      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_qyyYrN": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Dental care should <strong>not be a luxury</strong>",
            "title_highlight_color": "#47b5e9",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_xTU7RT": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Professional dental cleaning can cost <strong>$300-1,500</strong> and often requires anesthesia. Worse – many cats need it repeatedly because plaque keeps building up.</p><p>FreshWipes help you <strong>prevent tartar buildup </strong>at home, so your cat may never need that expensive procedure.</p><p><strong>For us, it's not about making money</strong> – it's about helping cats <strong>avoid painful dental problems.</strong></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
